<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beaumont-Hamel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beaumont-Hamel is a village in the Somme <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. On 1 July 1916, the first day of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-somme">Battle of the Somme</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-newfoundland-regiment">Newfoundland Regiment</a> attacked near the village and was almost wiped out in half an hour: of some 800 men who went forward, only 68 answered the roll call the next morning. The site is preserved as the Beaumont-Hamel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> Memorial, and 1 July is Memorial Day in Newfoundland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/labrador">Labrador</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beaumont-hamel.jpg" alt="Beaumont-Hamel" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Weglinde-Gordon Lawson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beaumont_4.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
